# Database / Local storage mounts
#
# Anchored to the repository root. Written as bare `data/` these rules matched
# a directory of that name at any depth, so `server/internal/data/` -- a Go
# package -- was ignored, and a new source file added to it was silently left
# out of every commit (the files already tracked there kept working, which is
# what hid it). The runtime directories that are not at the root are named
# explicitly instead.
/postgres_data/
/backups/
/data/
/mariadb_data/
# TLS material the server generates for itself at runtime, including private
# keys: ignored deliberately, and never to be committed.
server/internal/api/data/
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# Logs
*.log

# Distribution artifacts
dist/
